    "title": "Where Is John F. Kennedy Jr. Really Buried? All About Burial at Sea with Carolyn & Lauren Bessette",
    "text": "The finale of the limited series Love Story is now streaming on Hulu and it covers the deaths of John F. Kennedy Jr., his wife Carolyn Bessette, and her sister Lauren Bessette. JFK Jr, Carolyn, and Lauren tragically died in a plane crash on July 16, 1999 while traveling to Martha’s Vineyard. The small plane crashed into the Atlantic Ocean, just off the coast of the vineyard. Their bodies were recovered on July 21 and their burials took place one day later. The finale episode shows the tensions between the Kennedy and Bessette families while trying to decide where to bury the bodies. Keep reading to find out more… It has been reported that the Kennedy family wanted to bury John and Carolyn at the family plot in Massachusetts, but Lauren wasn’t allowed to be buried there as she wasn’t a member of the family. The Bessette family did not want the sisters to be separated. JFK Jr.‘s former assistant RoseMarie Terenzio wrote in her 2024 book that she suggested to Caroline Kennedy that they should be cremated and buried together. “I said, ‘Caroline, I think you should cremate them, and they should all stay together. I think John would want that.’ She wanted to honor her brother,” Terenzio wrote in the book (via People). It was decided that John, Carolyn, and Lauren would be cremated and buried together at sea. Their ashes were scattered in the waters off Martha’s Vineyard, just one day after their bodies were recovered. CNN reported in 1999, “The final resting place for JFK Jr., his wife and her sister was off Martha’s Vineyard, not far from where they died instantly last Friday when the aircraft piloted by Kennedy plunged into the ocean.” 17 family members from the Kennedy and Bessette families were on board the USS Briscoe for the ceremony. The show has been criticized by John‘s nephew, who calls the series a “grotesque display.”",
